Problem:
Simplify $(2-2i)(5+5i)$, where $i^2 = -1.$

Solution:
answer:  We can use the distributive property to simplify the expression $(2-2i)(5+5i)$:

\begin{align*}
(2-2i)(5+5i) &= 2(5) + 2(5i) - 2i(5) - 2i(5i) \\
&= 10 + 10i - 10i - 10i^2 \\
&= 10 + 10i - 10i - 10(-1) \\
&= 10 + 10i - 10i + 10 \\
&= 20 + 0i \\
&= \boxed{20}.
\end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $20$. I hope it is correct.
