Problem:
Simplify $(5-3i)(-4+3i)$.

Solution:
answer:  To simplify the expression \((5-3i)(-4+3i)\), we will use the distributive property (also known as the FOIL method for binomials):

\begin{align*}
(5-3i)(-4+3i) &= 5(-4) + 5(3i) - 3i(-4) + 3i(3i) \\
&= -20 + 15i + 12i + 9i^2 \\
&= -20 + 15i + 12i - 9(-1) \quad \text{(since } i^2 = -1 \text{)} \\
&= -20 + 15i + 12i + 9 \\
&= -11 + 27i.
\end{align*}

Therefore, the simplified form of the expression is \(\boxed{-11 + 27i}\).

Final Answer: The final answer is \(-11 + 27i\). I hope it is correct.
