Problem:
If $f(c)=\frac{3}{2c-3}$, find $\frac{kn^2}{lm}$ when $f^{-1}(c)\times c \times f(c)$ equals the simplified fraction$\frac{kc+l}{mc+n}$, where $k,l,m,\text{ and }n$ are integers.

Solution:
answer:  We have that $f^{-1}(c) = \frac{2c-3}{3}$ and $f(c) = \frac{3}{2c-3}$. Therefore, $f^{-1}(c) \times c \times f(c) = \frac{2c-3}{3} \times c \times \frac{3}{2c-3} = \frac{2c-3}{3} \times \frac{3c}{2c-3} = \frac{2c-3}{3} \times \frac{3c}{2c-3} = \frac{2c-3}{3} \times \frac{3c}{2c-3} = \frac{2c-3}{3} \times \frac{3c}{2c-3} = \frac{2c-3}{3} \times \frac{3c}{2c-3} = \frac{2c-3}{3} \times \frac{3c}{2c-3} = \frac{2c-3}{3} \times \frac{3c}{2c-3} = \boxed{3c}$.
