Problem:
Connie is starting an exercise program. On June 1, she will do 25 sit-ups. Each day after that, she will increase her number of sit-ups by four. On which date during the month of June will Connie first do more than 100 sit-ups in one day?

Solution:
answer:  To determine the date on which Connie first does more than 100 sit-ups in one day, we need to analyze the pattern of her sit-up count.

On June 1, Connie does 25 sit-ups. Each subsequent day, she increases her number of sit-ups by 4. Therefore, the number of sit-ups she does on day \( n \) can be expressed as:

\[ 25 + 4(n-1) \]

We need to find the smallest \( n \) such that:

\[ 25 + 4(n-1) > 100 \]

First, solve the inequality:

\[ 25 + 4(n-1) > 100 \]
\[ 4(n-1) > 75 \]
\[ n-1 > \frac{75}{4} \]
\[ n-1 > 18.75 \]
\[ n > 19.75 \]

The smallest integer greater than 19.75 is 20. Therefore, Connie will first do more than 100 sit-ups is on June 20.
