Problem:
Evaluate $531^2 - 2\cdot 531\cdot 530 + 530^2$.

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression $531^2 - 2\cdot 531\cdot 530 + 530^2$ as $(531 - 530)^2$. 

Now, we can use the binomial theorem to expand $(531 - 530)^2$:

\begin{align*}
(531 - 530)^2 &= 531^2 - 2\cdot 531\cdot 530 + 530^2 \\
&= 531^2 - 2\cdot 531\cdot 530 + 530^2 \\
&= 531^2 - 2\cdot 531\cdot 530 + 530^2 \\
&= 531^2 - 2\cdot 531\cdot 530 + 530^2 \\
&= 531^2 - 2\cdot 531\cdot 530 + 530^2 \\
&= (531 - 530)^2 = \boxed{1}.
\end{align*}
====================

