Problem:
Compute $\dbinom{22}{19}$.

Solution:
answer:  The binomial coefficient $\dbinom{22}{19}$ is defined as $\frac{22!}{19! \cdot 3!}$. We can simplify this by canceling out the common terms in the numerator and the denominator:

\begin{align*}
\dbinom{22}{19} &= \frac{22!}{19! \cdot 3!} \\
&= \frac{22 \cdot 21 \cdot 20 \cdot 19!}{19! \cdot 3!} \\
&= \frac{22 \cdot 21 \cdot 20}{3!} \\
&= \frac{22 \cdot 21 \cdot 20}{3 \cdot 2 \cdot 1} \\
&= \frac{22 \cdot 21 \cdot 20}{6} \\
&= \frac{9240}{6} \\
&= \boxed{1540}.
\end{align*}

Therefore, $\dbinom{22}{19} = \boxed{1540}$.
Final Answer: The final answer is $1540$.
