Problem:
What is the volume of a pyramid whose base is one face of a cube of side length $2$, and whose apex is the center of the cube? Give your answer in simplest form.

[asy]
import three;
triple A,B,C,D,EE,F,G,H;
A = (0,0,0);
B = (1,0,0);
C = (1,1,0);
D= (0,1,0);
EE = (0,0,1);
F = B+EE;
G = C + EE;
H = D + EE;
O = G/2;
draw(surface(B--O--C--cycle),red,nolight);
draw(surface(C--O--D--cycle),red+white,nolight);
draw(B--C--D);
draw(B--A--D,dashed);
draw(EE--F--G--H--EE);
draw(A--EE,dashed);
draw(B--F);
draw(C--G);
draw(D--H);
draw(A--O--C,dashed);
draw(B--O--D,dashed);
dot(A); dot(B); dot(C); dot(D); dot(EE); dot(F); dot(G); dot(H); dot(O);
[/asy]

Solution:
answer:  The base of the pyramid is a square with side length $2$, so its area is $2^2 = 4$. The height of the pyramid is the distance from the center of the cube to the plane of the base. Since the base is a face of the cube, the height is the same as the distance from the center of the cube to the plane of the base. This distance is the same as the distance from the center of the cube to the center of the base, which is half the side length of the cube, or $2/2 = 1$. Therefore, the volume of the pyramid is $\frac{1}{3} \cdot 4 \cdot 1 = \boxed{1}$.
Final Answer: The final answer is $1$. I hope it is correct.
====================

