Problem:
There exist constants $r,$ $s,$ and $t$ so that
\[p(n) = rp(n - 1) + sp(n - 2) + tp(n - 3)\]for any quadratic polynomial $p(x),$ and any integer $n.$  Enter the ordered triple $(r,s,t).$

Solution:
answer:  Let $p(x) = ax^2 + bx + c.$  Then
\begin{align*}
p(n) &= an^2 + bn + c, \\
p(n - 1) &= a(n - 1)^2 + b(n - 1) + c = an^2 - 2an + a + bn - b + c, \\
p(n - 2) &= a(n - 2)^2 + b(n - 2) + c = an^2 - 4an + 4a + bn - 2b + c, \\
p(n - 3) &= a(n - 3)^2 + b(n - 3) + c = an^2 - 6an + 9a + bn - 3b + c.
\end{align*}
Comparing coefficients, we get
\begin{align*}
r &= -1, \\
s &= -2, \\
t &= 3.
\end{align*}
Therefore, the ordered triple $(r,s,t)$ is
\[\boxed{(-1, -2, 3)}.
Final Answer: The final answer is $(-1, -2, 3)$. I hope it is correct.
