Problem:
The number $$\sqrt{104\sqrt6+468\sqrt{10}+144\sqrt{15}+2006}$$can be written as $a\sqrt2+b\sqrt3+c\sqrt5$, where $a$, $b$, and $c$ are positive integers.  Find $a\cdot b\cdot c.$

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the expression inside the square root as follows:

\begin{align*}
\sqrt{104\sqrt6+468\sqrt{10}+144\sqrt{15}+2006} &= \sqrt{104\sqrt{2\cdot3}+468\sqrt{2\cdot5}+144\sqrt{3\cdot5}+2006} \\
&= \sqrt{104\sqrt{6}+468\sqrt{10}+144\sqrt{15}+2006} \\
&= \sqrt{104\sqrt{6}+468\sqrt{10}+144\sqrt{15}+2006} \\
&= \sqrt{104\sqrt{6}+468\sqrt{10}+144\sqrt{15}+2006} \\
&= \sqrt{104\sqrt{6}+468\sqrt{10}+144\sqrt{15}+2006} \\
&= \boxed{1440}.
\end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $1440$. I hope it is correct.
