Problem:
If $a,b,c$ are positive integers less than $13$ such that \begin{align*}
2ab+bc+ca&\equiv 0\pmod{13}\\
ab+2bc+ca&\equiv 6abc\pmod{13}\\
ab+bc+2ca&\equiv 8abc\pmod {13}
\end{align*}then determine the remainder when $a+b+c$ is divided by $13$.

Solution:
answer:  We can rewrite the given congruences as follows:
\begin{align*}
2ab+bc+ca&\equiv 0\pmod{13}\\
ab+2bc+ca&\equiv 6abc\pmod{13}\\
ab+bc+2ca&\equiv 8abc\pmod{13}
\end{align*}
Adding these congruences, we get
\begin{align*}
(2ab+bc+ca)+(ab+2bc+ca)+(ab+bc+2ca)&\equiv 0+6abc+8abc\pmod{13}\\
4ab+4bc+4ca&\equiv 14abc\pmod{13}
\end{align*}
Dividing both sides by $4$, we get
\begin{align*}
ab+bc+ca&\equiv 3abc\pmod{13}
\end{align*}
Therefore, $a+b+c\equiv 3abc\pmod{13}$. Since $a,b,c$ are positive integers less than $13$, we have $3abc\equiv 0\pmod{13}$.

Final Answer: The remainder when $a+b+c$ is divided by $13$ is $\boxed{0}$.
====================

