Problem:
If the pattern shown continues, what is the letter in the $2010$th position? MATHLETEMATHLETEMATHLETE...

Solution:
answer:  To determine the letter in the 2010th position of the sequence "MATHLETEMATHLETEMATHLETE...", we first need to identify the repeating pattern. The sequence "MATHLETEMATHLETE" repeats every 10 letters.

To find the position of the 2010th letter within one complete cycle of the sequence, we calculate the remainder when 2010 is divided by 10:

\[ 2010 \div 10 = 201 \text{ remainder } 0 \]

This means that 2010 is exactly divisible by 10, so the 2010th letter corresponds to the 10th letter in the sequence "MATHLETEMATHLETE".

The 10th letter in the sequence "MATHLETEMATHLETE" is "E".

Therefore, the letter in the 2010th position is \(\boxed{E}\).
