Problem:
Find the remainder when $$33818^2 + 33819^2 + 33820^2 + 33821^2 + 33822^2$$is divided by 17.

Solution:
answer:  We can use modular arithmetic to simplify the problem. First, we find the remainder of each number when divided by 17:

\begin{align*}
33818 &\equiv 0 \pmod{17}, \\
33819 &\equiv 1 \pmod{17}, \\
33820 &\equiv 2 \pmod{17}, \\
33821 &\equiv 3 \pmod{17}, \\
33822 &\equiv 4 \pmod{17}.
\end{align*}

Now, we square these remainders and sum them up modulo 17:

\begin{align*}
33818^2 + 33819^2 + 33820^2 + 33821^2 + 33822^2 &\equiv 0^2 + 1^2 + 2^2 + 3^2 + 4^2 \\
&\equiv 0 + 1 + 4 + 9 + 16 \\
&\equiv 30 \equiv \boxed{6} \pmod{17}.
\end{align*}
