Problem:
Find the sum of the digits of the base-8 expression for $8888_{10}$.

Solution:
answer:  First, we need to convert $8888_{10}$ to base-8. We do this by repeatedly dividing the number by 8 and keeping track of the remainders.

\begin{align*}
8888 \div 8 &= 1111 \text{ remainder } 0 \\
1111 \div 8 &= 138 \text{ remainder } 11 \\
138 \div 8 &= 17 \text{ remainder } 2 \\
17 \div 8 &= 2 \text{ remainder } 1 \\
2 \div 8 &= 0 \text{ remainder } 2 \\
\end{align*}

Reading the remainders from bottom to top, we get the base-8 representation of $8888_{10}$ as $21220_8$.

Next, we find the sum of the digits of $21220_8$:

$$2 + 1 + 2 + 2 + 0 = 7$$

Therefore, the sum of the digits of $8888$ in base-8 is $\boxed{7}$.
