Problem:
It takes Michael 0.30 hours to walk to school. How many seconds does it take him to walk to school?

Solution:
answer:  To determine how many seconds it takes Michael to walk to school, we need to convert the time from hours to seconds. We know that:

\[ 1 \text{ hour} = 3600 \text{ seconds} \]

Given that it takes Michael 0.30 hours to walk to school, we can convert this time to seconds by multiplying 0.30 by 3600:

\[ 0.30 \text{ hours} \times 3600 \text{ seconds/hour} = 1080 \text{ seconds} \]

Therefore, it takes Michael \(\boxed{1080}\) seconds to walk to school.
