Problem:
Four typists can type a total of 600 memos in three days. At that rate, how many memos can three typists type in one day?

Solution:
answer:  To determine how many memos three typists can type in one day, we first need to find the rate at which one typist types. We know that four typists can type 600 memos in three days. Therefore, the total number of memos typed by four typists in one day is:

\[
\frac{600 \text{ memos}}{3 \text{ days}} = 200 \text{ memos per day}
\]

Since four typists can type 200 memos in one day, one typist can type:

\[
\frac{200 \text{ memos per day}}{4 \text{ typists}} = 50 \text{ memos per day}
\]

Now, if one typist can type 50 memos in one day, three typists can type:

\[
3 \text{ typists} \times 50 \text{ memos per day per typist} = 150 \text{ memos per day}
\]

Therefore, three typists can type \( \boxed{150} \) memos in one day.
====================

