Problem:
Add 313.9 to 12.6. Express the result as a decimal.

Solution:
answer:  To add 313.9 and 12.6, we can align the decimal points and add the numbers column by column:

\[
\begin{array}{r}
  313.9 \\
+  12.6 \\
\hline
\end{array}
\]

First, add the tenths place:

\[
\begin{array}{r}
  313.9 \\
+  12.6 \\
\hline
  325.5 \\
\end{array}
\]

Next, add the units place:

\[
\begin{array}{r}
  313.9 \\
+  12.6 \\
\hline
  326.5 \\
\end{array}
\]

Finally, add the tens place:

\[
\begin{array}{r}
  313.9 \\
+  12.6 \\
\hline
  326.5 \\
\end{array}
\]

So, the sum of 313.9 and 12.6 is \(\boxed{326.5}\).
