Problem:
Compute
\[\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^{2016}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We have that
\[
\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}.
\]
Therefore,
\[
\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^4 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^2)^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & 4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^2 = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}.
\]
Thus,
\[
\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}^{2016} = \begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}.
\]
The final answer is \boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 3 & -4 \\ 1 & -1 \end{pmatrix}}.
