Problem:
Evaluate
\[\begin{vmatrix} 0 & b - a & c - a \\ a - b & 0 & c - b \\ a - c & b - c & 0 \end{vmatrix}.\]

Solution:
answer:  To evaluate the determinant of the given matrix, we can use the properties of determinants. Specifically, we will use the fact that the determinant of a matrix with a row (or column) of all zeros is zero.

The given matrix is:
\[
\begin{vmatrix} 0 & b - a & c - a \\ a - b & 0 & c - b \\ a - c & b - c & 0 \end{vmatrix}
\]

We observe that the third row of the matrix is entirely zeros. Therefore, the determinant of the matrix is:
\[
\mathbf{0}
\]

To confirm, let's consider the third row:
\[
\begin{pmatrix} a - c & b - c & 0 \end{pmatrix}
\]

Since the third row is all zeros, the determinant of the entire matrix is:
\[
\det \begin{pmatrix} 0 & b - a & c - a \\ a - b & 0 & c - b \\ a - c & b - c & 0 \end{pmatrix} = 0
\]

Thus, the final answer for the determinant evaluation is:
\[
\boxed{0}
\]
