Problem:
Find all possible values of the determinant of
\[\begin{pmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{pmatrix},\]as $x$ ranges over all real numbers (where the determinant is defined).

Solution:
answer:  We can compute the determinant of the given matrix as follows:
\begin{align*}
\det \begin{pmatrix} \sec^2 x & 1 & 1 \\ \cos^2 x & \cos^2 x & \csc^2 x \\ 1 & \cos^2 x & \cot^2 x \end{pmatrix} &= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \csc^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x \\
&= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x \\
&= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x \\
&= \sec^2 x \cos^2 x \cot^2 x - \cos^2 x \sin^2 x - \cos^2 x \cot^2 x \\
&= \boxed{0}.
\end{align*}

Final Answer: The final answer is $0$.
====================

