Problem:
For positive real numbers $x,$ $y,$ and $z,$ none of which are equal to 1, find
\[\begin{vmatrix} 1 & \log_x y & \log_x z \\ \log_y x & 1 & \log_y z \\ \log_z x & \log_z y & 1 \end{vmatrix}.\]

Solution:
answer:  We can expand the determinant along the first row:
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix} 1 & \log_x y & \log_x z \\ \log_y x & 1 & \log_y z \\ \log_z x & \log_z y & 1 \end{vmatrix} &= 1 \begin{vmatrix} 1 & \log_y z \\ \log_z y & 1 \end{vmatrix} - \log_x y \begin{vmatrix} \log_y x & \log_y z \\ \log_z x & 1 \end{vmatrix} + \log_x z \begin{vmatrix} \log_y x & 1 \\ \log_z x & \log_z y \end{vmatrix} \\
&= 1 \cdot (1 - \log_y z \log_z y) - \log_x y \cdot (\log_y x \log_z y - \log_y z \log_z x) + \log_x z \cdot (\log_y x \log_z y - \log_z x) \\
&= 1 - 0 + 0 \\
&= \boxed{1}.
\end{align*}The final answer is 1. I hope it is correct.
