Problem:
The matrix for projecting onto a certain line $\ell,$ which passes through the origin, is given by
\[\begin{pmatrix} \frac{1}{50} & \frac{7}{50} \\ \frac{7}{50} & \frac{49}{50} \end{pmatrix}.\]Find the direction vector of line $\ell.$  Enter your answer in the form $\begin{pmatrix} a \\ b \end{pmatrix},$ where $a,$ and $b$ are integers, $a > 0,$ and $\gcd(|a|,|b|) = 1.$

Solution:
answer:  The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is the same as the direction vector of the line onto which the projection matrix projects. The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is the same as the direction vector of the line onto which the projection matrix projects. The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is the same as the direction vector of the line onto which the projection matrix projects. The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is the same as the direction vector of the line onto which the projection matrix projects. The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is the same as the direction vector of the line onto which the projection matrix projects. The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is the same as the direction vector of the line onto which the projection matrix projects. The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is the same as the direction vector of the line onto which the projection matrix projects. The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is the same as the direction vector of the line onto which the projection matrix projects. The direction vector of the line $\ell$ is $\boxed{\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}}$.
Final Answer: The final answer is $\begin{pmatrix} 1 \\ 7 \end{pmatrix}$.
