Problem:
Simplify $$2\cos^2(\log(2009)i)+i\sin(\log(4036081)i).$$Note: The logarithms are with respect to base $e.$

Solution:
answer:  First, we simplify the expression inside the cosine and sine functions.

$$\log(2009)i = \log(2009) + i\pi$$
$$\log(4036081)i = \log(4036081) + i\pi$$

Next, we use the properties of logarithms to simplify the expression.

$$\log(2009) = \log(2009^2) = 2\log(2009)$$
$$\log(4036081) = \log(2009^2) = 2\log(2009)$$

Now, we substitute these values back into the expression.

$$2\cos^2(\log(2009)i) + i\sin(\log(4036081)i) = 2\cos^2(\log(2009) + i\pi) + i\sin(2\log(2009) + i\pi)$$

Since the cosine and sine functions are periodic with period $2\pi$, we can simplify the expression using the periodicity.

$$\boxed{0}$$
