Problem:
Let $x_1,$ $x_2,$ $x_3,$ $y_1,$ $y_2,$ and $y_3$ be real numbers such that
\begin{align*}
(x_1 - x_2)^2 + (y_1 - y_2)^2 &= 9, \\
(x_1 - x_3)^2 + (y_1 - y_3)^2 &= 16, \\
(x_2 - x_3)^2 + (y_2 - y_3)^2 &= 25.
\end{align*}Find $\begin{vmatrix} x_1 & y_1 & 1 \\ x_2 & y_2 & 1 \\ x_3 & y_3 & 1 \end{vmatrix}^2.$

Solution:
answer:  We have that
\begin{align*}
\begin{vmatrix} x_1 & y_1 & 1 \\ x_2 & y_2 & 1 \\ x_3 & y_3 & 1 \end{vmatrix} &= x_1 y_2 - y_1 x_2 + x_2 y_3 - y_2 x_3 + x_3 y_1 - y_3 x_1 \\
&= x_1 y_2 - y_1 x_2 + x_2 y_3 - y_2 x_3 + x_3 y_1 - y_3 x_1 \\
&= (x_1 - x_2)(y_2 - y_1) + (x_2 - x_3)(y_3 - y_2) + (x_3 - x_1)(y_1 - y_3) \\
&= -x_1 y_2 - x_2 y_3 - x_3 y_1.
\end{align*}Therefore, the determinant is $0$, and so its square is $\boxed{0}$.
Final Answer: The final answer is $0$. I hope it is correct.
